	abstract = {Photovoltaic (PV) modules offer an efficient method for generating power from renewable energy in various locations. Characteristics of PV panels can be affected by a number of factors, including changes in radiation, partial shading, temperature, and the voltage at the terminals. Apart from the operating voltage, all of these factors rely on nature and are not readily changeable. It is essential to ensure efficient voltage regulation at the terminals in order to optimize power output from PV modules. There are several Maximum Power Point Tracking (MPPT) techniques available for PV modules, however, it is essential to have an integrating mechanism in place to guarantee optimal operation in any given situation. In order to reach a best location to exhibits more power during partial shading, Whale Optimization Algorithm (WOA) is developed. Further, Sliding Mode Control (SMC) associated with Artificial Neural Network (ANN) has the ability to quickly produce the desired reference signal for converter. A battery storage device is connected to store energy from PV for releasing when needed by load. The battery is connected at load bus through a bidirectional dc circuit. In order to avoid an extra circuit, the control method of bidirectional dc circuit is linked by MPPT algorithm. Hence it can acts as a MPPT device and the control method is designed with the help of WOA associated ANN based SMC. Therefore, combining WOA, ANN, SMC has the potential to improve the MPPT capacity to produce additional energy, despite changes in temperature and irradiance. In order to achieve more accurate outcomes, the proposed model is equipped with a Hardware-in- the-Loop (HIL) setup. © 2025 IEEE.},
