	abstract = {Power supplies through off-grid systems are more popular due to their requirement at many locations worldwide. Among many, renewable energy sources supplied off-grid systems are highly recommended for multiple purposes including reducing pollution, long life, easy access, low maintenance, etc. Hence, battery integrated hybrid renewable systems based off-grid power supply model is developed in this paper with a novel control methodology. In this research, we concentrated on the techno-economical viability and ideal configuration of a hybrid microhydro-PV-wind-diesel-battery unit intended to provide electricity to a standard village situated in a remote location. Our objective was to accomplish electrification at the lowest possible cost, while also considering the limitations related to environmental pollutant emissions. The performance and economic efficiency of the system were assessed based on several key factors, including net present cost (NPC), surplus electricity, cost of energy (COE), operational and maintenance expenses (O & M), capacity deficits, fuel consumption rates and costs for generators, loads fulfillment, as well as savings in CO2 and other pollutant gas emissions. Matlab and HOMER simulations based results are demonstrated the priority of the proposed method. © 2026 IEEE.},
