	affiliations = {Vardhaman College of Engineering, Department of Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning, Hyderabad, India; Vardhaman College of Engineering, Department of Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Hyderabad, India},
	abstract = {In an instance when fears about personal safety are growing, especially for the weaker members of society like the physically impaired, inventive technological solutions are essential. This study describes a multifunctional self-defense gear that combines cloud computing, Internet of Things (IoT) devices, and machine learning (ML) algorithms to lessen potential threats. The add-on uses a pulse sensor to recognize high heart rates that could be a sign of danger. This allows a camera to be activated in order to analyze the threat. The ML algorithms use facial gesture analysis and prerecorded photographs of known criminals to evaluate the scenario and, if needed, trigger a small pepper spray module for immediate defense. The gadget also has a GPS tracker built in to notify local authorities of the user's location in the happening of an emergency. The captured video is securely kept on a cloud-based stand that is only accessible to the owner, escalating the usefulness of the add-on as a prophylactic and possible proof lest of an urgent situation. This essay describes the self-defense accessory's development, application, and assessment, emphasizing how it might deeply improve private security for people of all ability levels.  © 2024 IEEE.},
