	affiliations = {Department of Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Renganayagi Varatharaj College of Engineering, Sivakasi, India; Department of Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Kamaraj College of Engineering and Technology, Virudhunagar, India; Department of Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Vardhaman College of Engineering, Hyderabad, India; Department of Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Chennai Institute of Technology, Chennai, India; Department of Electrical, Electronic and Systems Engineering, Faculty Engineering and Built Environment, Universiti Kebangsaan Malaysia, Bangi, Malaysia},
	abstract = {This paper presents a Hybrid Coupled Matching (HCM) reconfiguration algorithm for efficient global maximum power point tracking (GMPPT) in photovoltaic systems under partial shading conditions. By integrating sorting-based decision logic, switching control, and embedded reconfiguration, the proposed method improves tracking accuracy, convergence speed, and system robustness. The proposed HCM algorithm improves tracking accuracy, convergence speed, and robustness against dynamic irradiance variations. A 4 × 4 PV array comprising sixteen 10 W modules is modeled in MATLAB/Simulink and experimentally validated under diverse shading patterns. Quantitative results demonstrate that, under PSC, the proposed HCM configuration achieves the maximum output power of 80 W, compared with 45 W obtained using the conventional Total Cross-Tied (TCT) configuration, while reducing power losses from 113 W to 80 W. Furthermore, the HCM approach achieves performance enhancement ratios of 60.17%, 50.21%, 10.13%, and 44.31% over TCT, Adaptive Dynamic Reconfiguration (ADR), SUDOKU, and Couple Matching (CM) techniques, respectively, under short-and-wide PSCs. These results confirm that the proposed HCM strategy offers a computationally efficient, fast-converging, and robust solution for PV systems operating under complex and dynamic partial shading conditions. © 2026 The Chinese Institute of Engineers.},
	author_keywords = {couple matching technique; hybrid couple matching; Partial shading; Power Enhancement; shade dispersion},
