	abstract = {Numerous renewable sources are integrating into power system network and increasing their number day by day worldwide. Integrating of high penetration of renewable energy sources can lead power system into considerable concerns over oscillations and stability. These problems can resolve by using an energy storage device with an appropriate control mechanism. However, a single energy storage device cannot be providing an efficient solution for all the problems. Hence, a hybrid energy storage system which consisting of a battery energy storage system (BESS) and a Synchronous Condenser (SC) is considered in this paper. This paper initially presents a sizing strategy grounded in techno-economic analysis, utilizing the Whale optimization technique. This approach aims to reduce the costs associated with the BESS-SC hybrid system while ensuring that the Rate of Change of Frequency (RoCoF) remains within an acceptable threshold. This paper subsequently presents a locating strategy aimed at determining the optimal site for the BESS-SC hybrid system. This strategy employs the Short Circuit Ratio (SCR) for location identification and is further validated through the Prony method, which utilizes eigenvalue and damping ratio analysis. Various responses are presented and analyzed by using Simulink on MATLAB platform. © 2026 IEEE.},
