	abstract = {The growing interest in Five Phase Induction Motors (FPIMs) can be attributed to their diverse range of applications, which encompass electric vehicles, advanced compressor systems, and marine propulsion, among others. Among many available drive control systems, Direct Torque Control Method (DTCM) is a powerful strategy to regulate speed, torque and flux within permissible limits of induction motors. However, conventional DTCMs are failed to regulate flux and speed in smoothly under drastically changes in the system due to not regulating flux with any controllers. Hence, the reference flux is obtained through a controller in proposed methodology presented in this paper. Moreover, conventional PI/PID controller cannot produce accurate output due to its fixed gains, hence TSK-Fuzzy controllers are used in this paper. Two TSK Fuzzy controllers are employed in the proposed DTCM where one is to produce reference torque and other is for reference flux. Additionally, the space vector pulse width modulation (SVPWM) technique is employed to generate the appropriate pulse sequence for a five leg inverter used in motor drive applications. A detailed design of TSK Fuzzy controller is also incorporated in this paper. In order to make speed sensorless controller, mathematical modeling is included to estimate speed of the motor to avoid physical sensor. Hardware - in the - Loop (HIL) technique is implemented on OPAL-RT platform to present various results similar to real time responses. © 2025 IEEE.},
