	abstract = {Frequency control of any hybrid Microgrid systems is playing a crucial role in maintaining power quality without any interrupts of power supply. This will be more attention during cyber threats. Hence, a novel methodology is suggested here with the help of optimization based control strategy. Power supplied by hybrid Photovoltaic (PV), wind power system, battery bank, flywheel energy system, fuel cell (i.e., hydrogen energy) and diesel generator based system can be a strong Microgrid. Hence, such kind of standalone Microgrid is considered in this paper for feasible analysis. In general, Fractional Order Proportional Integral-Derivative (FOPID) controllers are more effective than conventional PID controllers under sensitive changes in any Microgrid system. However, an appropriate online tuning of various parameters is required for FOPID controllers. Hence, Modified Advanced Whale Optimization (MAWO) method is implemented on FOPID controllers to achieve an efficient and effective response over any small change or sensitive control aspects. The suggested method efficiently reduces the effects of cyberinduced time-delay attacks, random assaults, and malware threats, while also dynamically adjusting to changes in the functioning of energy storage systems. Various results are presented by establishing Hardware - in the - Loop (HIL) concept. © 2026 IEEE.},
