	abstract = {Push-Pull DC converters are using for many applications including Maximum Power Point tracking (MPPT) device of a Photovoltaic (PV) system. Multiple PV modules are connected in a PV system, hence, partial shading effect will be causing on many modules. Unfortunately conventional Perturb and Observe (P&O) method approach cannot identify Global Maximum Power Point (GMPP) among multiple local maximums appear during partial shading conditions (PSCs). Hence, an efficient optimization method is required to reach GMPP among all maximum points. A Cocks Hens Chicken Optimization (CHCO) is implemented on MPPT of PV system to identify GMPP under PSCs. Hence, CHCO based MPPT algorithm is implemented on Push-Pull converter in this paper for PV applications under PSC. To achieve an effective control methodology, Artificial Neural Network (ANN) based controllers are utilized in the proposed control methodology. The proposed method is compared with Modified Grey Wolf Optimization (MGWO), Modified Invasive Weed Optimization (MIWO) and Whale Inspired Optimization (WIO) to enhance the significance of proposed approach. The system is developed in Hardware - in the - Loop (HIL) process on OPAL-RT platform to present various results.  © 2025 IEEE.},
