	abstract = {Microgrid systems rely on distribution generators are widely establishing worldwide. In order to maintain energy management in Microgrid systems, an energy storage unit like battery storage device must be required. For an AC Microgrid, a DC to AC circuit must be linked between battery system and AC bus. To manage or supply a quality power at AC bus, the converter associated with battery bank must be regulate both active and reactive power under prescribed standards. This control mechanism can also help to stabilize the power system under various circumstances. A grid connected AC Microgrid system is considered in this paper which is having battery storage system. A novel control methodology is developed in this article to regulate both active and reactive power at load bus for supplying the quality power. In order to confirm the effectiveness of the proposed control unit, a 5-kW gridconnected inverter has been constructed to showcase its capability for power smoothing and voltage regulation. For showcasing real-time responses, Hardware - in the - Loop (HIL) is established by using two OPAL-RT units. Various results are demonstrated the effectiveness of the suggested control methodology. © 2026 IEEE.},
