	abstract = {In this paper, the honey badger optimization algorithm (HBOA) tuned two degree-of-freedom (DOF) proportional-integral-derivative (PID) (2DOFPID) is presented as the frequency regulator to the interconnected power system (IPS). The operational performance of the suggested controller is tested on the IPS model of the multi-area diversified multifuel (MADMF) system in the literature. The analysis is conducted on the MADMF system subjected to the step load perturbation (SLP) of 10% in area-1. However, in order to obtain the stability analysis of the MADMF system near to practicality, the realistic constraints are deliberated with the generation units. The efficacy of the HBOA-tuned 2DOFPID performance is validated with other control approaches in the literature. Later, the MADMF system is integrated with the HVDC line, and the analysis is continued under the operation of the HBOA-tuned 2DOFPID regulator. The simulation results demonstrated that there is a significant improvement in the dynamical behavior of the MADMF system incorporated with the HVDC tie line. Finally, the system is targeted with different loading conditions to validate the robustness of the presented control approach.  © 2025 IEEE.},
