	abstract = {In the past few decades many different technologies have come to the fore that are able to produce a grid. In the past few decades there have been many technologies developed that can form a grid. Any converter controller that can control the terminal voltage at any time in time, suitable for both grid-following and grid-forming converter operation and for synchronous generation in the same converter system is called as grid-forming converter. It should make it easier to create scalable and decentralized AC power networks where the voltage and frequency are controlled by synergy amongst the grid-forming components. The goal of this research is to design an innovative control approach that can be developed to design the weather driven resources grid forming converters. For such purposes, a unique method is developed in this study, DQL jelly beluga controller. This work uses the hybrid jelly fish beluga optimization method to optimize the value of a sigmoid function which results in high efficiency of the controlled. In addition, the proposed study considers the renewable penetration to achieve grid stability and reliability. Furthermore, it is demonstrated that in the future generations, grid-forming converters are more essential than the grid-following converters if a rigorous analysis is performed. © 2026 IOP Publishing Ltd. All rights, including for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies, are reserved. This article is available under the terms of the IOP-Standard License.},
