	affiliations = {Institute of Aeronautical Engineering, Dept. of Computer Science Engg, Hyderabad, India; Aditya Degree College (women), Dept. of Computer Science Engg, Visakhapatnam, India; Cmrit, Dept of Eee, Hyderabad, India; Vardhaman College of Engg, Dept of Electrical and Electronics Engg, Hyderabad, India; Mohan Babu University, Dept of Electrical and Electronics Engg, Tirupati, India; Ss&c Fintech Services India, Pvt Ltd, India},
	abstract = {Massive MIMO technology is essential for addressing the growing demands of future wireless communication systems, including high user density, reliable connectivity, and energy efficiency. By employing large antenna arrays at base stations, massive MIMO enables simultaneous service to multiple users with enhanced spectral and energy efficiency, making it a cornerstone of 5G and beyond. This research evaluates the performance of three linear precoding techniques - vector-form Zero Forcing (ZF), Wiener Filter (WF), and Maximum Ratio Combining (MF) - in a single-cell downlink massive MIMO system under ideal channel conditions for single-antenna users. The analysis highlights that WF delivers superior spectral efficiency and lowest BER for smaller antenna arrays, while vector-form ZF approaches WF's energy efficiency as antenna count increases. With large antenna arrays, all three methods demonstrate comparable performance. This work underscores the importance of selecting the optimal precoding technique to ensure efficient and reliable system performance in massive MIMO networks.  © 2025 IEEE.},
