	abstract = {This paper investigates the convergence of hybrid electric vehicles (HEVs) and renewable energy sources for a sustainable future by unveiling their transformative potential within the automotive industry and the sustainable energy landscape. Recognized for efficiently utilizing internal combustion engines and electric power, HEVs serve as a pivotal bridge toward eco-friendly transportation. The study explores the innovative integration of HEVs with diverse renewable sources like solar, fuel cells, and wind. Leveraging energy from these sources extends HEVs’ electric range, diminishes reliance on fossil fuels, and substantially cuts greenhouse gas emissions. The technologies for capturing, storing, and utilizing renewable energy in HEV systems are examined. These bidirectional integrations enable HEVs not only to draw power from renewables but also to contribute excess energy back to the grid during idle periods, fostering a dynamic ecosystem that enhances energy resilience and grid stability. This comprehensive review highlights the integration of HEVs with renewable energy sources as a pivotal convergence for sustainable transportation. As HEVs stand at the intersection of traditional and fully electric vehicles, this study emphasizes their role in optimizing fuel efficiency and reducing emissions and calls for continued research and development to hasten the adoption of this integration, contributing to a greener and more sustainable transportation ecosystem. © 2024 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.},
