	abstract = {The integration of Natural Language Processing (NLP) into smart traffic systems offers a novel approach to enhancing real-time traffic management and optimization. This paper explores how NLP can be leveraged to interpret and analyze vast amounts of unstructured traffic-related data, such as social media updates, traffic reports, and incident logs. A key component of this approach is the use of a BERT (Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers) classifier, which enables more accurate extraction and classification of relevant traffic information from textual data. By processing this data in real time, the BERT-based NLP system can provide more precise traffic predictions, identify congestion patterns, and optimize traffic flow dynamically. The study highlights the potential of NLP, particularly through the use of BERT, in improving the efficiency and responsiveness of traffic management systems, ultimately leading to reduced travel times, lower emissions, and enhanced urban mobility. The app also includes user-friendly interfaces that allow drivers and city planners to access real-time updates, personalized route recommendations, and predictive analytics. The system's adaptability ensures that it can respond quickly to unexpected incidents, such as accidents or road closures, further enhancing urban mobility. The study highlights the transformation potential of this app in improving the efficiency and responsiveness of traffic management systems, ultimately leading to reduced travel times, lower emissions, and a significant improvement in overall urban transportation experiences.  © 2025 IEEE.},
