	abstract = {Solar energy is one of the most applied renewable sources because of environmental friendliness, minimal maintenance costs and capacity to sustain the increasing energy requirements. A solar photovoltaic system does not work only with the solar panels, but also with the mechanical support system and the reliability during the changes of the power. The paper provides a design and installation of a ground mounting solar support structure with an auxiliary power supply. The fabricated proposed structure involves the use of iron due to its strength, durability, and low cost. It is tailored to carry three solar panels with a fixed tilt of 22 degrees and this enables the panels to be fully exploited to the solar radiations during the day. The frame is 1690 mm x 3000 mm all round and it has internal support rods that make it structurally stable. Base plates and bolts ensure the anchoring is proper to resist against the wind and vibration and a distance of 15 mm between panels allows ventilation and thermal expansion. A parallel connected electrolytic capacitors based power source is added using parallel connected electrolytic capacitors to supply the short term backup when faced with a drop in voltage. The suggested solar system is a simple yet quality solution that can be applied to small-scale and rural solar solutions. © 2026 IEEE.},
