	abstract = {Switched or Variable Reluctance Motor (SRM) is a desirable substitute of broadly used synchronous and induction motors, due to its low-cost simple design, reliable operation, greater performance at high range speeds. The SRM pre-requisites a converter due to the double-salient formation for furnishing the independent control functions. The conventional Asymmetric converter is used to driving the SRM, but it is unsuitable because of high switch stress due to carrying input rated voltage, more loss, low efficiency, etc. These issues are counteracted by novel cascaded converter topologies controlled by attractive control objectives. But it requires more input DC sources which imply the size, cost, etc. This paper proposes a novel reduced DC sourced cascaded converter topologies to drive the SRM controlled by simplified Hysteresis Current Controller with low switch stress, attains low losses and high efficiency. The performance of proposed converter topology is verified with conventional converter topologies by using Matlab/Simulink tool and results are illustrated with comparisons. © 2020 SERSC.},
