	abstract = {India is divided into many areas, each with its own distinct characteristics such as sunshine exposure, energy consumption habits, and physical factors. The goal is to create specialized solar power plans that meet the individual needs of each place. This includes assessing parameters such as solar irradiation, energy demand, and available land or infrastructure for solar panel installation. By tailoring methods to the circumstances of each region, it guarantees that solar energy resources are deployed optimally, easing India's transition to sustainable and dependable energy sources. The study will conduct a comparative examination of solar power generation in five different Indian regions. This comparison considers a variety of measures, including the levelized cost of energy, yearly AC energy production, performance ratio, and simple payback period. The goal is to assess the effectiveness and efficiency of solar energy installations in these various locales. © 2025, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.},
