	affiliations = {Vardhaman College of Engineering, Department of EEE, Hyderabad, India},
	abstract = {In this project, the design and implementation of an energy efficient hybrid microgrid system based on the integration of solar photovoltaic (PV) and wind energy sources with a diesel generator as a backup power unit are presented. The primary goal of the suggested system is to maintain the solid and uninterrupted supply of power and optimize the utilization of diesel fuel and the total cost of operation. An intelligent, programmable control policy is constantly tracking the load demand together with the availability of the solar and wind resources to come up with an optimal operating schedule of the diesel generator. A doubly-fed induction generator (DFIG) is added to wind power, and the solar PV is made to connect directly to the DC bus of a back-To-back system of voltage source converter (VSC). It has a battery energy storage system (BES) that is incorporated via bidirectional buck-boost converter to handle the surplus supply of power as well as to assist the load demand during renewable lapse. A perturbed perturb and observe control algorithm is used to provide a maximum power extraction and a better fuel economy. The synchronized work of renewable sources, energy storage and diesel generator will help to make the system more efficient, decrease the number of greenhouse gases and decrease the fossil fuel dependence. The proposed microgrid is especially appropriate in isolated and unconnected areas that have low access to existing utility grids. The performance of the system is first checked with MATLAB/Simulink simulations. © 2026 IEEE.},
