	abstract = {This project is a Smart Solar DC Microgrid System based on ESP32, which is meant to be an intelligent control of the delivery of power to various household loads. The prototype is designed to have a solar panel, charge controller, and a battery bank to constitute a stable DC bus. Battery voltage and load current are monitored with voltage dividers and current sensors respectively by real-time monitoring of the system. The ESP32 constantly measures these parameters, voltage, current, and load status, and presents them both on a 16 × 2 LCD and Wi-Fi enabled IoT dashboard, which can be seen in the experimental results. The ESP32 is a decision maker which can act dynamically depending on the how much power available. The loads are switched on and off in a relay-based priority switching mechanism depending on the battery voltage and load current that the controller. The loads are categorized as: Essential Load (LED) - this is ON at any rate other than under very low voltage, Secondary Load (DC Fan) - may be turned on when the voltage is in medium or high range, Tertiary Load (DC Motor) - only loads in case there is sufficient power. The live readings during testing like Voltage A ≈ 6.5 V, Voltage B ≈ 6.6 V and currents of 1.6 - 1.7 A indicate that there was correct sensing and stable operation. On the whole, the system is well-integrated to use renewable energy, smart load management, and IoT-based monitoring, which is appropriate to use in microgrids within homes to ensure their reliability and energy efficiency. © 2026 IEEE.},
