	abstract = {Microgrid systems especially supplied by Photovoltaic (PV) modules are having a special interest due to its wide verity of applications and usages. In order to harvest more energy, an efficient mechanism along with a suitable converter must be incorporated in such Microgrid systems. A novel configuration of high gain boost converter is developed in this paper to utilize for PV system in Microgrid. The same converter is utilized as a Maximum Power Point Tracking (MPPT) device to harvest more energy as per changes in solar irradiance. In order to work MPPT converter effectively during the low irradiances, high gain boost convert is required which we proposed in this paper. The input side of the suggested converter utilizes a switched-inductor cell to minimize input current source ripples, a significant issue in PV systems designed for high-reliability applications. Furthermore, a switched-capacitor cell is implemented on the output side of the converter to enhance voltage gain and alleviate voltage stress on the power switches of the converter. This aspect is vital for extending the lifespan of both the PV panel and the components of the proposed converter, especially the semiconductor switches/components. Various results are examined through Hardware-in the-Loop (HIL). © 2026 IEEE.},
