	abstract = {Photovoltaic systems are gaining popularity as critical, secure, and widely available options for future energy provision. These systems' performance is impacted by both solar cell radiation and ambient temperature. This study looks at the usage of multiple controllers, notably fuzzy logic and the perturb and observe approach, to optimize the power output of a solar system. By combining these controllers with a DC-DC boost converter, the system may efficiently raise voltage, increasing battery charging efficiency. The fundamental goal of this research is to develop the effective controller for a solar system using these complicated control techniques. The Maximum Power Point Tracking (MPPT) approach is used to capture the most power from the solar system and power to the load. Fuzzy logic is used to increase the voltage output of a solar system, and the perturb and observe approach is used for MPPT control considerably improve the performance and dependability of solar systems. the proposed highbred technique maximizes energy extraction while also ensuring steady and efficient functioning in a variety of environmental situations. The findings of this study give vital insights for the creation of more efficient solar power systems, helping to progress sustainable energy technology. © 2025 IEEE.},
