	abstract = {This paper introduces an advanced detection algorithm based on YOLOv8 to challenge low accuracy high rates of missed detections and insufficient robustness in the detection of strip steel surface defects within complex industrial settings. Referred to as YOLO-KD, this algorithm builds on the YOLOv8n baseline model and enhances its performance through three primary modifications: feature fusion, feature extraction, and optimization of the loss function. That in the feature extraction phase the original C2f module is substituted with a C2f-KAN structure which significantly boosts the models capability to represent features. Thereby, the proposed method is improving its ability to extract defect characteristics for feature fusion the traditional. UpSample operator is creatively replaced with the Dynamic Upsampling Operator (DySample) which allows for more precise multi-scale feature fusion and effectively enhances the models performance in detecting minute defects against complex backgrounds. To finish in terms of optimization objectives, the CIoU loss function is replaced with InnerPIoU to further enhance the accuracy of defect location detection on strip steel surfaces. New results found from the NEU-DET dataset are indicating that the YOLO-KD algorithm suggestively exceeds the baseline model to achieve a recall rate of 75.2% (an increase of 4.3 percentage points), a mean Average Precision (mAP) of 77.5% (a rise of 2.1 percentage points) and an F 1 score of 75% (an improvement of 2.25 percentage points). The YOLO-KD algorithm proposed in this study achieves a frame per second (FPS) rate of 121.7. The proposed method demonstrates considerable advantages in performances, fulfilling the realtime demands to detect strip steel surface defects and highlighting its substantial engineering application values as compared to the industrial production line requirement of 30100 FPS. © 2026 IEEE.},
