	abstract = {In restructured environment, transmission congestion in power system is made by increasing the load demand. If the congestion is not harsh it can be relieved also by generation rescheduling. The congestion management trouble is to be dealt with some previous superior methods for a rigorously congested structure. In this paper, methods to alleviate congestion by generation rescheduling with installation of FACTS devices are presented. The congestion in the structure is attempted to be reassured by generation rescheduling alone. Among the different FACTS devices, Thyristor Controlled Series Compensator (TCSC) and Static Var Compensator is tested in this paper. Apart from relieving congestion, the other problems such as power loss and generation rate of the arrangement are also reduced simultaneously. Transmission System (FACTS) devices can be used to improve the voltage stability enhancement. The optimal locations and sizing of SVCs and TCSCs besides with generation rescheduling is carried out using Differential Evolution Programming and implemented on IEEE 30 Bus system for various loading conditions. © Research India Publications.},
